Tie rod assemblies for steering systems fall under heading 8708.94 (steering wheels, steering columns and steering boxes; parts thereof) in HTSUS. The relevant subheading is 8708.94.30 for "Parts" of steering components, with statistical suffixes under 8708.94.30 (formerly 8708.94.50/8708.94.75). Specifically, 8708.94.75 is "Other" within the steering parts, and 8708.94.7500 is the commonly used code for tie rod ends and assemblies.

The structure of 8708.94 is: 8708.94.10 for steering wheels, columns and boxes, and 8708.94.30 for parts of those. In the current schedule, 8708.94.30 is "Steering wheels, steering columns and steering boxes: Other: Parts" with a 10-digit suffix of 8708.94.3000 or similar, and 8708.94.75 is "Other." Tie rod ends are often classified in CBP rulings under 8708.94.7500 or 8708.94.7000. I'll go with 8708.94.7500.

{"hts_code": "8708.94.7500", "reason": "The assembled automotive tie rod assembly is a steering system part of motor vehicles, classified in heading 8708 under subheading 8708.94 as steering parts, in the 'other' provision."}
